import IUT.PaperIV.LocalFields.Logarithm
import IUT.PaperIV.LocalFields.Padic

/-!
# IUT IV, Propositions 1.2 and 1.3: the closed unit ball of the spectral norm is the ring of integers

Source: Mochizuki, *Inter-universal Teichmüller Theory IV*, Propositions 1.1 to 1.3, pages 9 to
12 of the April 2020 manuscript. Pages read for this file: 9, 10, 11 and 12. Pages checked against
rendered images: 9, 10, 11 and 12 (the normalization `ord(p) = 1`, the ring of integers `R_i` of a
finite extension `k_i` of `ℚ_p` and the order `𝔡_i` of the different on page 9; the ramification
index `e_i`, the constants `a_i`, `b_i`, the fractional ideals `p ^ λ · R_i` for `λ ∈ (1 / e_i) ℤ`
and assertion (i) of Proposition 1.2 on page 10; the proof of Proposition 1.2 on page 11;
Proposition 1.3 (i) on pages 11 and 12).

## The gap closed here

Two earlier files model the paper's local objects in two different ways.
`IUT.PaperIV.LocalFields.Padic` uses the ring of integers `integralClosure ℤ_[p] L` of a finite
extension `L` of `ℚ_[p]`, a prime `P` of it over `p` and Mathlib's `Ideal.ramificationIdx`.
`IUT.PaperIV.LocalFields.Logarithm` uses the spectral norm `‖·‖` on `L`, the closed unit ball as
ring of integers, the unit sphere as its units, and the ramification index only through the
hypothesis `hval : ‖x‖ < 1 → ‖x‖ ^ e ≤ 1 / p`. This file proves that the two models agree, for a
finite extension `L` of `ℚ_[p]` (a field with a finite-dimensional `ℚ_[p]`-algebra structure and a
compatible `ℤ_[p]`-algebra structure) and its spectral norm `spectralNorm ℚ_[p] L`.

What is proved:

1. `padicBridge_norm_le_one_iff_isIntegral`: `‖x‖ ≤ 1` if and only if `x` is integral over
   `ℤ_[p]`. The spectral norm of `x` is the spectral value of the minimal polynomial of `x` over
   `ℚ_[p]`, which is at most one exactly when all coefficients lie in `ℤ_[p]`
   (`spectralValue_le_one_iff`); since `ℤ_[p]` is integrally closed, this holds exactly when `x`
   is integral (`minpoly.isIntegrallyClosed_eq_field_fractions'`,
   `Polynomial.lifts_and_degree_eq_and_monic`). Hence `padicBridge_integralClosure_eq_unitBall`:
   the closed unit ball is `integralClosure ℤ_[p] L` as a set.
2. `padicBridge_isUnit_iff`, `padicBridge_range_units_eq_unitSphere`: the unit sphere is the image
   of the unit group of `integralClosure ℤ_[p] L`.
3. The value group and the ramification index:
   * `padicBridge_isLocalRing`, `padicBridge_isDiscreteValuationRing`: the ring of integers is
     local with maximal ideal `{‖x‖ < 1}` (`padicBridge_mem_maximalIdeal_iff`), hence a discrete
     valuation ring;
   * `padicBridge_maximalIdeal_liesOver`, `padicBridge_prime_eq_maximalIdeal`: its maximal ideal
     lies over `p`, and it is the only prime ideal over `p`; so every statement of `Padic.lean`
     about a prime `P` over `p` is about this ideal, and `differentOrder ℤ_[p] R P` is the paper's
     `𝔡_i`;
   * `padicBridge_uniformizer`: with `e = P.ramificationIdx ℤ_[p]`, there is a uniformizer `ϖ`
     with `P = (ϖ)`, `(p) = (ϖ) ^ e` as ideals, `‖ϖ‖ ^ e = 1 / p`, every nonzero `x` of `L` has
     `‖x‖ = ‖ϖ‖ ^ k` for an integer `k`, and `‖x‖ ≤ ‖ϖ‖` when `‖x‖ < 1`;
   * `padicBridge_norm_range_units`: the image of `‖·‖` on `Lˣ` is `{p ^ (k / e) | k ∈ ℤ}`;
   * `padicBridge_hval`, `padicBridge_ramificationIdx_le_of_hval`: `hval` holds for
     `e = P.ramificationIdx ℤ_[p]`, and for no smaller natural number;
   * `padicBridge_closedBall_eq_range_mul`, `padicBridge_exists_norm_eq_rpow`: for
     `λ ∈ (1 / e) ℤ` the paper's fractional ideal `p ^ λ · R`, generated by an element of
     `ord = λ`, exists and equals the closed ball `{‖z‖ ≤ p ^ (-λ)}` used in `Logarithm.lean`;
     `padicBridge_a_eq_int_div`, `padicBridge_b_eq_int_div`: `a_i` and `-b_i` lie in
     `(1 / e_i) ℤ`.
4. Corollaries without the hypothesis `hval`, for `R = integralClosure ℤ_[p] L` and
   `e = P.ramificationIdx ℤ_[p]`:
   * `padicBridge_extLogUnit_image_bounds`: IUT IV Proposition 1.2 (i),
     `p ^ a · R ⊆ log (R^×) ⊆ p ^ (-b) · R`, with `R^×` the unit group of the integral closure and
     `p ^ λ · R` written as a closed ball;
   * `padicBridge_extLogUnit_image_fractionalIdeal`: the same with `p ^ a · R` and `p ^ (-b) · R`
     the fractional ideals `y · R`, `z · R` generated by elements `y`, `z` of norms `p ^ (-a)`,
     `p ^ b`, which exist;
   * `padicBridge_extLogUnit_image_eq_of_le`: the equality `log (R^×) = p ^ (1 / e) · R` for
     `p > 2` and `e ≤ p - 2`;
   * `padicBridge_extLogShell_bounds`: the bounds `p* p ^ a · R ⊆ I ⊆ p* p ^ (-b) · R` for the
     log-shell `I` of IUT III Definition 1.1;
   * `padicBridge_log_bounds_and_differentOrder`: Proposition 1.2 (i) together with
     `𝔡 ≥ (e - 1) / e` (Proposition 1.3 (i) for `k_0 = ℚ_p`) and `𝔡 + a ≥ 1` (`p > 2`),
     `𝔡 + a ≥ 2` (`p = 2`), all with the same `e` and the same ideal `P`.

Not formalized here: the uniqueness of the norm on `L` (the spectral norm is used throughout; by
Mathlib's `spectralNorm_unique` it is the only power-multiplicative algebra norm extending the
`p`-adic norm, but no statement here uses another norm); Proposition 1.2 (ii) to (iv), which need
the tensor products `R_I` of Proposition 1.1; the statements of Proposition 1.4, whose log-volumes
are not formalized (its per-index arithmetic, `Proposition1_4.a_add_b_le`, takes only `p` and `e`
and needs nothing from this file).
-/

open Ideal

namespace IUT.PaperIV.LocalFields

section Bridge

variable (p : ℕ) [Fact p.Prime] (L : Type*) [Field L] [Algebra ℚ_[p] L]
  [FiniteDimensional ℚ_[p] L] [Algebra ℤ_[p] L] [IsScalarTower ℤ_[p] ℚ_[p] L]

/-! ### 1. The closed unit ball is the integral closure of `ℤ_p` -/

/-- **The closed unit ball is the ring of integers, pointwise**: for `x` in a finite extension `L`
of `ℚ_[p]`, the spectral norm satisfies `‖x‖ ≤ 1` if and only if `x` is integral over `ℤ_[p]`. -/
theorem padicBridge_norm_le_one_iff_isIntegral (x : L) :
    letI := spectralNorm.normedField ℚ_[p] L
    ‖x‖ ≤ 1 ↔ IsIntegral ℤ_[p] x := by
  let := spectralNorm.normedField ℚ_[p] L
  have hxi : IsIntegral ℚ_[p] x := Algebra.IsIntegral.isIntegral x
  show spectralNorm ℚ_[p] L x ≤ 1 ↔ _
  rw [spectralNorm, spectralValue_le_one_iff (minpoly.monic hxi)]
  constructor
  · intro h
    have hl : minpoly ℚ_[p] x ∈ Polynomial.lifts (algebraMap ℤ_[p] ℚ_[p]) := by
      rw [Polynomial.lifts_iff_coeff_lifts]
      intro n
      exact ⟨⟨_, h n⟩, rfl⟩
    obtain ⟨q, hq, -, hqm⟩ := Polynomial.lifts_and_degree_eq_and_monic hl (minpoly.monic hxi)
    refine ⟨q, hqm, ?_⟩
    rw [IsScalarTower.algebraMap_eq ℤ_[p] ℚ_[p] L, ← Polynomial.eval₂_map, hq, ← Polynomial.aeval_def]
    exact minpoly.aeval ℚ_[p] x
  · intro hx n
    rw [minpoly.isIntegrallyClosed_eq_field_fractions' ℚ_[p] hx, Polynomial.coeff_map,
      PadicInt.algebraMap_apply]
    exact ((minpoly ℤ_[p] x).coeff n).2

/-- Membership in `integralClosure ℤ_[p] L` is `‖x‖ ≤ 1` for the spectral norm. -/
theorem padicBridge_mem_integralClosure_iff (x : L) :
    letI := spectralNorm.normedField ℚ_[p] L
    x ∈ integralClosure ℤ_[p] L ↔ ‖x‖ ≤ 1 :=
  Iff.trans (mem_integralClosure_iff ℤ_[p] L) (padicBridge_norm_le_one_iff_isIntegral p L x).symm

/-- **The closed unit ball of the spectral norm is `integralClosure ℤ_[p] L`** as a set. -/
theorem padicBridge_integralClosure_eq_unitBall :
    letI := spectralNorm.normedField ℚ_[p] L
    ((integralClosure ℤ_[p] L : Subalgebra ℤ_[p] L) : Set L) = {x : L | ‖x‖ ≤ 1} :=
  Set.ext fun x => padicBridge_mem_integralClosure_iff p L x

/-- Every element of the ring of integers has spectral norm at most one. -/
theorem padicBridge_norm_le_one (y : integralClosure ℤ_[p] L) :
    letI := spectralNorm.normedField ℚ_[p] L
    ‖(y : L)‖ ≤ 1 :=
  (padicBridge_mem_integralClosure_iff p L y).1 y.2

/-! ### 2. The unit sphere is the unit group -/

/-- An element of the ring of integers is a unit if and only if its spectral norm is one. -/
theorem padicBridge_isUnit_iff (x : integralClosure ℤ_[p] L) :
    letI := spectralNorm.normedField ℚ_[p] L
    IsUnit x ↔ ‖(x : L)‖ = 1 := by
  let := spectralNorm.normedField ℚ_[p] L
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨u, rfl⟩
    have hmul : ((u : integralClosure ℤ_[p] L) : L) *
        (((u⁻¹ : (integralClosure ℤ_[p] L)ˣ) : integralClosure ℤ_[p] L) : L) = 1 := by
      exact congrArg (fun y : integralClosure ℤ_[p] L => (y : L)) u.mul_inv
    have h1 := congrArg norm hmul
    rw [norm_mul, norm_one] at h1
    have ha := padicBridge_norm_le_one p L (u : integralClosure ℤ_[p] L)
    have hb := padicBridge_norm_le_one p L ((u⁻¹ : (integralClosure ℤ_[p] L)ˣ) :
      integralClosure ℤ_[p] L)
    nlinarith [norm_nonneg ((u : integralClosure ℤ_[p] L) : L),
      norm_nonneg (((u⁻¹ : (integralClosure ℤ_[p] L)ˣ) : integralClosure ℤ_[p] L) : L)]
  · intro h
    have hx0 : (x : L) ≠ 0 := by
      intro h0
      rw [h0, norm_zero] at h
      exact zero_ne_one h
    have hinv : (x : L)⁻¹ ∈ integralClosure ℤ_[p] L :=
      (padicBridge_mem_integralClosure_iff p L _).2 (by rw [norm_inv, h, inv_one])
    refine isUnit_iff_exists_inv.mpr ⟨⟨_, hinv⟩, Subtype.ext ?_⟩
    show (x : L) * (x : L)⁻¹ = 1
    exact mul_inv_cancel₀ hx0

/-- **The unit sphere is the unit group of the ring of integers**:
`{x | ‖x‖ = 1}` is the image of `(integralClosure ℤ_[p] L)ˣ` in `L`. -/
theorem padicBridge_range_units_eq_unitSphere :
    letI := spectralNorm.normedField ℚ_[p] L
    Set.range (fun u : (integralClosure ℤ_[p] L)ˣ => ((u : integralClosure ℤ_[p] L) : L)) =
      {x : L | ‖x‖ = 1} := by
  let := spectralNorm.normedField ℚ_[p] L
  ext x
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨u, rfl⟩
    exact (padicBridge_isUnit_iff p L _).1 u.isUnit
  · intro hx
    have hx' : ‖x‖ = 1 := hx
    have hmem : x ∈ integralClosure ℤ_[p] L :=
      (padicBridge_mem_integralClosure_iff p L x).2 hx'.le
    obtain ⟨u, hu⟩ := (padicBridge_isUnit_iff p L ⟨x, hmem⟩).2 hx'
    refine ⟨u, ?_⟩
    show ((u : integralClosure ℤ_[p] L) : L) = x
    rw [hu]

/-- An element of the ring of integers is a nonunit if and only if its spectral norm is `< 1`. -/
theorem padicBridge_mem_nonunits_iff (x : integralClosure ℤ_[p] L) :
    letI := spectralNorm.normedField ℚ_[p] L
    x ∈ nonunits (integralClosure ℤ_[p] L) ↔ ‖(x : L)‖ < 1 := by
  let := spectralNorm.normedField ℚ_[p] L
  rw [mem_nonunits_iff, padicBridge_isUnit_iff]
  exact ⟨fun h => lt_of_le_of_ne (padicBridge_norm_le_one p L x) h, fun h => h.ne⟩

/-! ### 3. The local ring, the uniformizer and the ramification index -/

omit [Algebra ℤ_[p] L] [IsScalarTower ℤ_[p] ℚ_[p] L] in
/-- `‖p‖ = 1 / p` in `L` for the spectral norm. -/
theorem padicBridge_norm_natCast_p :
    letI := spectralNorm.normedField ℚ_[p] L
    ‖((p : ℕ) : L)‖ = (p : ℝ)⁻¹ := by
  let := spectralNorm.normedField ℚ_[p] L
  rw [← map_natCast (algebraMap ℚ_[p] L) p]
  exact (spectralNorm_extends (p : ℚ_[p])).trans Padic.norm_p

/-- The spectral norm of the image of a `p`-adic integer `c` is `‖c‖`. -/
theorem padicBridge_norm_algebraMap_padicInt (c : ℤ_[p]) :
    letI := spectralNorm.normedField ℚ_[p] L
    ‖algebraMap ℤ_[p] L c‖ = ‖c‖ := by
  let := spectralNorm.normedField ℚ_[p] L
  rw [IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply ℤ_[p] ℚ_[p] L]
  exact spectralNorm_extends _

/-- **The ring of integers of a finite extension of `ℚ_[p]` is local**: its nonunits, the elements
of spectral norm `< 1`, are closed under addition by the ultrametric inequality. -/
theorem padicBridge_isLocalRing : IsLocalRing (integralClosure ℤ_[p] L) := by
  let := spectralNorm.normedField ℚ_[p] L
  refine IsLocalRing.of_nonunits_add fun a b ha hb => ?_
  rw [padicBridge_mem_nonunits_iff] at ha hb ⊢
  exact (isNonarchimedean_spectralNorm (K := ℚ_[p]) (a : L) (b : L)).trans_lt (max_lt ha hb)

/-- **The maximal ideal of the ring of integers is `{‖x‖ < 1}`.** -/
theorem padicBridge_mem_maximalIdeal_iff (x : integralClosure ℤ_[p] L) :
    haveI := padicBridge_isLocalRing p L
    letI := spectralNorm.normedField ℚ_[p] L
    x ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (integralClosure ℤ_[p] L) ↔ ‖(x : L)‖ < 1 := by
  have := padicBridge_isLocalRing p L
  rw [IsLocalRing.mem_maximalIdeal]
  exact padicBridge_mem_nonunits_iff p L x

/-- The element `p` of the ring of integers is nonzero and not a unit. -/
theorem padicBridge_natCast_p_ne_zero_not_isUnit :
    ((p : ℕ) : integralClosure ℤ_[p] L) ≠ 0 ∧ ¬ IsUnit ((p : ℕ) : integralClosure ℤ_[p] L) := by
  let := spectralNorm.normedField ℚ_[p] L
  have hn : ‖(((p : ℕ) : integralClosure ℤ_[p] L) : L)‖ = (p : ℝ)⁻¹ := by
    push_cast
    exact padicBridge_norm_natCast_p p L
  have hlt : (p : ℝ)⁻¹ < 1 := inv_lt_one_of_one_lt₀ (by exact_mod_cast (Fact.out : p.Prime).one_lt)
  refine ⟨fun h0 => ?_, fun hu => ?_⟩
  · rw [h0] at hn
    simp only [ZeroMemClass.coe_zero, norm_zero] at hn
    exact (inv_pos.mpr (by exact_mod_cast (Fact.out : p.Prime).pos : (0 : ℝ) < p)).ne' hn.symm
  · rw [padicBridge_isUnit_iff, hn] at hu
    exact hlt.ne hu

/-- **The ring of integers is a discrete valuation ring**: a local Dedekind domain that is not a
field (`p` is a nonzero nonunit). -/
theorem padicBridge_isDiscreteValuationRing :
    IsDiscreteValuationRing (integralClosure ℤ_[p] L) := by
  have := padicBridge_isLocalRing p L
  have := isDedekindDomain_ringOfIntegers_padic p L
  have hnf : ¬ IsField (integralClosure ℤ_[p] L) := by
    intro hF
    obtain ⟨h0, hu⟩ := padicBridge_natCast_p_ne_zero_not_isUnit p L
    obtain ⟨b, hb⟩ := hF.mul_inv_cancel h0
    exact hu (isUnit_iff_exists_inv.mpr ⟨b, hb⟩)
  exact ((IsDiscreteValuationRing.TFAE (integralClosure ℤ_[p] L) hnf).out 1 3).mpr
    (show IsDedekindDomain (integralClosure ℤ_[p] L) from inferInstance)

/-- **The maximal ideal of the ring of integers lies over `p`**: its contraction to `ℤ_[p]` is the
maximal ideal `pℤ_p`. -/
theorem padicBridge_maximalIdeal_liesOver :
    haveI := padicBridge_isLocalRing p L
    (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (integralClosure ℤ_[p] L)).LiesOver (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal ℤ_[p]) := by
  have := padicBridge_isLocalRing p L
  let := spectralNorm.normedField ℚ_[p] L
  refine ⟨Ideal.ext fun c => ?_⟩
  rw [Ideal.mem_comap, padicBridge_mem_maximalIdeal_iff, IsLocalRing.mem_maximalIdeal,
    PadicInt.mem_nonunits]
  show ‖c‖ < 1 ↔ ‖algebraMap ℤ_[p] L c‖ < 1
  rw [padicBridge_norm_algebraMap_padicInt]

/-- **Uniqueness of the prime over `p`**: every prime ideal of the ring of integers lying over
`pℤ_p` is the maximal ideal. -/
theorem padicBridge_prime_eq_maximalIdeal (P : Ideal (integralClosure ℤ_[p] L)) [P.IsPrime]
    [P.LiesOver (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal ℤ_[p])] :
    haveI := padicBridge_isLocalRing p L
    P = IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (integralClosure ℤ_[p] L) := by
  have := padicBridge_isLocalRing p L
  have := isDedekindDomain_ringOfIntegers_padic p L
  have := isTorsionFree_ringOfIntegers_padic p L
  have hP0 : P ≠ ⊥ :=
    ne_bot_of_liesOver_of_ne_bot (IsDiscreteValuationRing.not_a_field ℤ_[p]) P
  exact IsLocalRing.eq_maximalIdeal (Ideal.IsPrime.isMaximal inferInstance hP0)

/-- Every prime `P` of the ring of integers over `p` is `{‖x‖ < 1}`. -/
theorem padicBridge_mem_prime_iff (P : Ideal (integralClosure ℤ_[p] L)) [P.IsPrime]
    [P.LiesOver (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal ℤ_[p])] (x : integralClosure ℤ_[p] L) :
    letI := spectralNorm.normedField ℚ_[p] L
    x ∈ P ↔ ‖(x : L)‖ < 1 := by
  have := padicBridge_isLocalRing p L
  rw [padicBridge_prime_eq_maximalIdeal p L P]
  exact padicBridge_mem_maximalIdeal_iff p L x

/-- In the ring of integers, a nonzero `y` has `‖y‖ = ‖ϖ‖ ^ n` for a natural number `n` and any
irreducible `ϖ`, with `n ≥ 1` when `‖y‖ < 1`. -/
theorem padicBridge_norm_eq_pow_of_ne_zero {ϖ : integralClosure ℤ_[p] L} (hϖ : Irreducible ϖ)
    {y : integralClosure ℤ_[p] L} (hy : y ≠ 0) :
    letI := spectralNorm.normedField ℚ_[p] L
    ∃ n : ℕ, ‖(y : L)‖ = ‖(ϖ : L)‖ ^ n ∧ (‖(y : L)‖ < 1 → 1 ≤ n) := by
  let := spectralNorm.normedField ℚ_[p] L
  have := padicBridge_isDiscreteValuationRing p L
  obtain ⟨n, u, hu⟩ := IsDiscreteValuationRing.eq_unit_mul_pow_irreducible hy hϖ
  have hun : ‖((u : integralClosure ℤ_[p] L) : L)‖ = 1 :=
    (padicBridge_isUnit_iff p L _).1 u.isUnit
  have hnorm : ‖(y : L)‖ = ‖(ϖ : L)‖ ^ n := by
    rw [hu]
    push_cast
    rw [norm_mul, hun, one_mul, norm_pow]
  refine ⟨n, hnorm, fun hlt => ?_⟩
  rcases Nat.eq_zero_or_pos n with h0 | h0
  · rw [hnorm, h0, pow_zero] at hlt
    exact absurd hlt (lt_irrefl 1)
  · exact h0

/-- **Ramification index from a factorization**: if `p = u ϖ ^ n` in the ring of integers with
`ϖ` irreducible and `u` a unit, then `n` is the ramification index of every prime `P` over `p`.
-/
theorem padicBridge_ramificationIdx_eq (P : Ideal (integralClosure ℤ_[p] L)) [P.IsPrime]
    [P.LiesOver (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal ℤ_[p])] {ϖ : integralClosure ℤ_[p] L} (hϖ : Irreducible ϖ) {n : ℕ}
    (hn : Associated ((p : ℕ) : integralClosure ℤ_[p] L) (ϖ ^ n)) :
    P.ramificationIdx ℤ_[p] = n := by
  have := padicBridge_isLocalRing p L
  have := padicBridge_isDiscreteValuationRing p L
  have := isDedekindDomain_ringOfIntegers_padic p L
  have := isTorsionFree_ringOfIntegers_padic p L
  have hPspan : P = Ideal.span {ϖ} := by
    rw [padicBridge_prime_eq_maximalIdeal p L P]
    exact (IsDiscreteValuationRing.irreducible_iff_uniformizer ϖ).1 hϖ
  have hmap : (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal ℤ_[p]).map (algebraMap ℤ_[p] (integralClosure ℤ_[p] L)) = P ^ n := by
    rw [PadicInt.maximalIdeal_eq_span_p, Ideal.map_span, Set.image_singleton, map_natCast,
      hPspan, Ideal.span_singleton_pow, Ideal.span_singleton_eq_span_singleton]
    exact hn
  have hP0 : P ≠ ⊥ := by
    rw [hPspan, Ne, Ideal.span_singleton_eq_bot]
    exact hϖ.ne_zero
  have hne : (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal ℤ_[p]).map (algebraMap ℤ_[p] (integralClosure ℤ_[p] L)) ≠ ⊥ := by
    rw [hmap]
    exact pow_ne_zero n hP0
  rw [IsDedekindDomain.ramificationIdx_eq_multiplicity (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal ℤ_[p]) P hne, hmap]
  exact multiplicity_pow_self_of_prime (Ideal.prime_of_isPrime hP0 inferInstance) n

/-- **Uniformizer and value group** of a finite extension `L` of `ℚ_[p]` with its spectral norm,
in terms of the ramification index `e = P.ramificationIdx ℤ_[p]` of the prime `P` over `p`:
there is an irreducible `ϖ` of the ring of integers `R` with `P = (ϖ)`, `(p) = (ϖ) ^ e` as ideals
of `R`, `0 < ‖ϖ‖ < 1`, `‖ϖ‖ ^ e = 1 / p`, `‖x‖ = ‖ϖ‖ ^ k` with `k ∈ ℤ` for every nonzero `x`, and
`‖x‖ ≤ ‖ϖ‖` whenever `‖x‖ < 1`. -/
theorem padicBridge_uniformizer (P : Ideal (integralClosure ℤ_[p] L)) [P.IsPrime]
    [P.LiesOver (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal ℤ_[p])] :
    letI := spectralNorm.normedField ℚ_[p] L
    ∃ ϖ : integralClosure ℤ_[p] L, Irreducible ϖ ∧ P = Ideal.span {ϖ} ∧
      Ideal.span {((p : ℕ) : integralClosure ℤ_[p] L)} =
        Ideal.span {ϖ} ^ P.ramificationIdx ℤ_[p] ∧
      0 < ‖(ϖ : L)‖ ∧ ‖(ϖ : L)‖ < 1 ∧ ‖(ϖ : L)‖ ^ P.ramificationIdx ℤ_[p] = (p : ℝ)⁻¹ ∧
      (∀ x : L, x ≠ 0 → ∃ k : ℤ, ‖x‖ = ‖(ϖ : L)‖ ^ k) ∧
      (∀ x : L, ‖x‖ < 1 → ‖x‖ ≤ ‖(ϖ : L)‖) := by
  let := spectralNorm.normedField ℚ_[p] L
  have := padicBridge_isLocalRing p L
  have := padicBridge_isDiscreteValuationRing p L
  obtain ⟨ϖ, hϖ⟩ := IsDiscreteValuationRing.exists_irreducible (integralClosure ℤ_[p] L)
  obtain ⟨hp0, -⟩ := padicBridge_natCast_p_ne_zero_not_isUnit p L
  obtain ⟨m, u, hu⟩ := IsDiscreteValuationRing.eq_unit_mul_pow_irreducible hp0 hϖ
  have hassoc : Associated ((p : ℕ) : integralClosure ℤ_[p] L) (ϖ ^ m) := by
    rw [hu]
    exact associated_unit_mul_left (ϖ ^ m) (u : integralClosure ℤ_[p] L) u.isUnit
  have he := padicBridge_ramificationIdx_eq p L P hϖ hassoc
  have hϖ0 : (ϖ : L) ≠ 0 := by
    intro h
    exact hϖ.ne_zero (Subtype.ext h)
  have hpos : 0 < ‖(ϖ : L)‖ := norm_pos_iff.mpr hϖ0
  have hlt1 : ‖(ϖ : L)‖ < 1 := (padicBridge_mem_nonunits_iff p L ϖ).1 hϖ.not_isUnit
  have hpe : ‖(ϖ : L)‖ ^ m = (p : ℝ)⁻¹ := by
    obtain ⟨n, hn, -⟩ := padicBridge_norm_eq_pow_of_ne_zero p L hϖ hp0
    have hn' : ‖(((p : ℕ) : integralClosure ℤ_[p] L) : L)‖ = ‖(ϖ : L)‖ ^ m := by
      rw [hu]
      push_cast
      rw [norm_mul, (padicBridge_isUnit_iff p L _).1 u.isUnit, one_mul, norm_pow]
    rw [← hn']
    push_cast
    exact padicBridge_norm_natCast_p p L
  have hle : ∀ x : L, ‖x‖ < 1 → ‖x‖ ≤ ‖(ϖ : L)‖ := by
    intro x hx
    rcases eq_or_ne x 0 with rfl | hx0
    · rw [norm_zero]; exact hpos.le
    have hmem : x ∈ integralClosure ℤ_[p] L :=
      (padicBridge_mem_integralClosure_iff p L x).2 hx.le
    have hy : (⟨x, hmem⟩ : integralClosure ℤ_[p] L) ≠ 0 := by
      intro h; exact hx0 (congrArg Subtype.val h)
    obtain ⟨n, hn, hn1⟩ := padicBridge_norm_eq_pow_of_ne_zero p L hϖ hy
    have hn1' := hn1 hx
    show ‖x‖ ≤ _
    rw [show ‖x‖ = ‖(ϖ : L)‖ ^ n from hn]
    exact pow_le_of_le_one hpos.le hlt1.le (by omega)
  refine ⟨ϖ, hϖ, ?_, ?_, hpos, hlt1, he ▸ hpe, ?_, hle⟩
  · rw [padicBridge_prime_eq_maximalIdeal p L P]
    exact (IsDiscreteValuationRing.irreducible_iff_uniformizer ϖ).1 hϖ
  · rw [he, Ideal.span_singleton_pow, Ideal.span_singleton_eq_span_singleton]
    exact hassoc
  · intro x hx0
    rcases le_or_gt ‖x‖ 1 with hx1 | hx1
    · have hmem : x ∈ integralClosure ℤ_[p] L :=
        (padicBridge_mem_integralClosure_iff p L x).2 hx1
      have hy : (⟨x, hmem⟩ : integralClosure ℤ_[p] L) ≠ 0 := by
        intro h; exact hx0 (congrArg Subtype.val h)
      obtain ⟨n, hn, -⟩ := padicBridge_norm_eq_pow_of_ne_zero p L hϖ hy
      exact ⟨n, by rw [zpow_natCast]; exact hn⟩
    · have hi : ‖x⁻¹‖ ≤ 1 := by
        rw [norm_inv]; exact (inv_lt_one_of_one_lt₀ hx1).le
      have hmem : x⁻¹ ∈ integralClosure ℤ_[p] L :=
        (padicBridge_mem_integralClosure_iff p L _).2 hi
      have hy : (⟨x⁻¹, hmem⟩ : integralClosure ℤ_[p] L) ≠ 0 := by
        intro h; exact inv_ne_zero hx0 (congrArg Subtype.val h)
      obtain ⟨n, hn, -⟩ := padicBridge_norm_eq_pow_of_ne_zero p L hϖ hy
      refine ⟨-(n : ℤ), ?_⟩
      have hn' : ‖x‖⁻¹ = ‖(ϖ : L)‖ ^ n := by rw [← norm_inv]; exact hn
      rw [zpow_neg, zpow_natCast, ← hn', inv_inv]

/-- **`hval` holds for the ramification index**: every `x` with `‖x‖ < 1` has
`‖x‖ ^ e ≤ 1 / p`, `e = P.ramificationIdx ℤ_[p]`. This is the hypothesis of
`IUT.PaperIV.LocalFields.Logarithm` for this `e`. -/
theorem padicBridge_hval (P : Ideal (integralClosure ℤ_[p] L)) [P.IsPrime]
    [P.LiesOver (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal ℤ_[p])] :
    letI := spectralNorm.normedField ℚ_[p] L
    ∀ x : L, ‖x‖ < 1 → ‖x‖ ^ P.ramificationIdx ℤ_[p] ≤ (p : ℝ)⁻¹ := by
  let := spectralNorm.normedField ℚ_[p] L
  obtain ⟨ϖ, -, -, -, -, -, hpe, -, hle⟩ := padicBridge_uniformizer p L P
  intro x hx
  rw [← hpe]
  exact pow_le_pow_left₀ (norm_nonneg _) (hle x hx) _

/-- **No smaller exponent satisfies `hval`**: if `‖x‖ ^ e' ≤ 1 / p` for every `x` with `‖x‖ < 1`,
then `P.ramificationIdx ℤ_[p] ≤ e'`. So the ramification index is the least natural number `e`
for which the hypothesis `hval` of `IUT.PaperIV.LocalFields.Logarithm` holds. -/
theorem padicBridge_ramificationIdx_le_of_hval (P : Ideal (integralClosure ℤ_[p] L)) [P.IsPrime]
    [P.LiesOver (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal ℤ_[p])] {e' : ℕ}
    (h : letI := spectralNorm.normedField ℚ_[p] L
      ∀ x : L, ‖x‖ < 1 → ‖x‖ ^ e' ≤ (p : ℝ)⁻¹) :
    P.ramificationIdx ℤ_[p] ≤ e' := by
  let := spectralNorm.normedField ℚ_[p] L
  obtain ⟨ϖ, -, -, -, hpos, hlt1, hpe, -, -⟩ := padicBridge_uniformizer p L P
  have h' := h (ϖ : L) hlt1
  rw [← hpe] at h'
  exact (pow_le_pow_iff_right_of_lt_one₀ hpos hlt1).1 h'

/-- `‖ϖ‖ = p ^ (-1 / e)` for a uniformizer, from `‖ϖ‖ ^ e = 1 / p`. -/
theorem padicBridge_rpow_of_pow_eq {t : ℝ} (ht : 0 ≤ t) {e : ℕ} (he : e ≠ 0)
    (h : t ^ e = (p : ℝ)⁻¹) : t = (p : ℝ) ^ (-(1 / (e : ℝ))) := by
  have hp0 : (0 : ℝ) < p := by exact_mod_cast (Fact.out : p.Prime).pos
  have he0 : (e : ℝ) ≠ 0 := Nat.cast_ne_zero.mpr he
  refine (pow_left_inj₀ ht (Real.rpow_nonneg hp0.le _) he).1 ?_
  rw [h, ← Real.rpow_natCast, ← Real.rpow_mul hp0.le,
    show -(1 / (e : ℝ)) * (e : ℝ) = -1 by field_simp, Real.rpow_neg_one]

/-- **The value group**: the image of the spectral norm on `Lˣ` is `{p ^ (k / e) | k ∈ ℤ}` with
`e = P.ramificationIdx ℤ_[p]`; in the paper's normalization, `ord(Lˣ) = (1 / e) ℤ`. -/
theorem padicBridge_norm_range_units (P : Ideal (integralClosure ℤ_[p] L)) [P.IsPrime]
    [P.LiesOver (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal ℤ_[p])] :
    letI := spectralNorm.normedField ℚ_[p] L
    Set.range (fun x : Lˣ => ‖(x : L)‖) =
      Set.range (fun k : ℤ => (p : ℝ) ^ ((k : ℝ) / (P.ramificationIdx ℤ_[p] : ℝ))) := by
  let := spectralNorm.normedField ℚ_[p] L
  have := isDedekindDomain_ringOfIntegers_padic p L
  have := isTorsionFree_ringOfIntegers_padic p L
  obtain ⟨ϖ, -, -, -, hpos, -, hpe, hval, -⟩ := padicBridge_uniformizer p L P
  set e := P.ramificationIdx ℤ_[p] with he_def
  have he1 : 0 < e := ramificationIdx_pos_of_liesOver (IsDiscreteValuationRing.not_a_field ℤ_[p]) P
  have hp0 : (0 : ℝ) < p := by exact_mod_cast (Fact.out : p.Prime).pos
  have he0 : (e : ℝ) ≠ 0 := Nat.cast_ne_zero.mpr he1.ne'
  have hr := padicBridge_rpow_of_pow_eq p hpos.le he1.ne' hpe
  have hz : ∀ k : ℤ, ‖(ϖ : L)‖ ^ k = (p : ℝ) ^ (((-k : ℤ) : ℝ) / (e : ℝ)) := by
    intro k
    rw [hr, ← Real.rpow_intCast, ← Real.rpow_mul hp0.le]
    congr 1
    push_cast
    field_simp
  ext t
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨x, rfl⟩
    obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := hval (x : L) x.ne_zero
    exact ⟨-k, by simp only; rw [hk, hz]⟩
  · rintro ⟨k, rfl⟩
    have hϖ0 : (ϖ : L) ≠ 0 := norm_pos_iff.mp hpos
    refine ⟨Units.mk0 ((ϖ : L) ^ (-k)) (zpow_ne_zero _ hϖ0), ?_⟩
    simp only [Units.val_mk0]
    rw [norm_zpow, hz, neg_neg]

/-- For every `λ ∈ (1 / e) ℤ` there is an element `y` of `L` with `ord(y) = λ`, i.e.
`‖y‖ = p ^ (-λ)`; here `λ = -k / e`. -/
theorem padicBridge_exists_norm_eq_rpow (P : Ideal (integralClosure ℤ_[p] L)) [P.IsPrime]
    [P.LiesOver (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal ℤ_[p])] (k : ℤ) :
    letI := spectralNorm.normedField ℚ_[p] L
    ∃ y : L, y ≠ 0 ∧ ‖y‖ = (p : ℝ) ^ ((k : ℝ) / (P.ramificationIdx ℤ_[p] : ℝ)) := by
  let := spectralNorm.normedField ℚ_[p] L
  have h : (p : ℝ) ^ ((k : ℝ) / (P.ramificationIdx ℤ_[p] : ℝ)) ∈
      Set.range (fun x : Lˣ => ‖(x : L)‖) := by
    rw [padicBridge_norm_range_units p L P]
    exact ⟨k, rfl⟩
  obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ := h
  exact ⟨x, x.ne_zero, hx⟩

/-- **Fractional ideals are closed balls**: for `y ≠ 0`, the fractional ideal `y · R` generated
by `y` over the ring of integers `R` is the closed ball `{z | ‖z‖ ≤ ‖y‖}`. With
`‖y‖ = p ^ (-λ)` this is the paper's `p ^ λ · R`. -/
theorem padicBridge_closedBall_eq_range_mul {y : L} (hy : y ≠ 0) :
    letI := spectralNorm.normedField ℚ_[p] L
    {z : L | ‖z‖ ≤ ‖y‖} = Set.range (fun r : integralClosure ℤ_[p] L => y * (r : L)) := by
  let := spectralNorm.normedField ℚ_[p] L
  have hy0 : 0 < ‖y‖ := norm_pos_iff.mpr hy
  ext z
  constructor
  · intro hz
    have hz' : ‖z‖ ≤ ‖y‖ := hz
    have hmem : z / y ∈ integralClosure ℤ_[p] L := by
      rw [padicBridge_mem_integralClosure_iff, norm_div, div_le_one hy0]
      exact hz'
    exact ⟨⟨z / y, hmem⟩, mul_div_cancel₀ z hy⟩
  · rintro ⟨r, rfl⟩
    show ‖y * (r : L)‖ ≤ ‖y‖
    rw [norm_mul]
    exact mul_le_of_le_one_right hy0.le (padicBridge_norm_le_one p L r)

omit [Fact p.Prime] in
/-- `a_i ∈ (1 / e_i) ℤ`: `a = k / e` for an integer `k` (`k = ⌈e / (p - 2)⌉` for `p > 2`,
`k = 2e` for `p = 2`). -/
theorem padicBridge_a_eq_int_div {e : ℕ} (he : e ≠ 0) :
    ∃ k : ℤ, Proposition1_2.a p e = (k : ℝ) / (e : ℝ) := by
  have he0 : (e : ℝ) ≠ 0 := Nat.cast_ne_zero.mpr he
  unfold Proposition1_2.a
  split_ifs
  · exact ⟨2 * e, by push_cast; field_simp⟩
  · exact ⟨⌈(e : ℝ) / ((p : ℝ) - 2)⌉, by ring⟩

omit [Fact p.Prime] in
/-- `b_i ∈ (1 / e_i) ℤ`: `b = k / e` with `k = e ⌊log (p e / (p - 1)) / log p⌋ - 1`. -/
theorem padicBridge_b_eq_int_div {e : ℕ} (he : e ≠ 0) :
    ∃ k : ℤ, Proposition1_2.b p e = (k : ℝ) / (e : ℝ) := by
  have he0 : (e : ℝ) ≠ 0 := Nat.cast_ne_zero.mpr he
  refine ⟨e * ⌊Real.log ((p : ℝ) * e / ((p : ℝ) - 1)) / Real.log p⌋ - 1, ?_⟩
  unfold Proposition1_2.b
  push_cast
  field_simp

/-! ### 4. Corollaries for the ring of integers and the ramification index -/

/-- **IUT IV Proposition 1.2 (i)** (page 10) for a finite extension `L` of `ℚ_[p]`, with
`R_i = integralClosure ℤ_[p] L`, `R_i^×` its unit group and `e_i = P.ramificationIdx ℤ_[p]` for
the prime `P` over `p`: `p ^ a · R ⊆ log (R^×) ⊆ p ^ (-b) · R`, the fractional ideals written as
the closed balls `{‖z‖ ≤ p ^ (-a)}` and `{‖z‖ ≤ p ^ b}` (they are the fractional ideals,
`padicBridge_extLogUnit_image_fractionalIdeal`). No hypothesis on the norm remains. -/
theorem padicBridge_extLogUnit_image_bounds (P : Ideal (integralClosure ℤ_[p] L)) [P.IsPrime]
    [P.LiesOver (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal ℤ_[p])] :
    letI := spectralNorm.normedField ℚ_[p] L
    {z : L | ‖z‖ ≤ (p : ℝ) ^ (-Proposition1_2.a p (P.ramificationIdx ℤ_[p]))} ⊆
        extLogUnit '' Set.range
          (fun u : (integralClosure ℤ_[p] L)ˣ => ((u : integralClosure ℤ_[p] L) : L)) ∧
      extLogUnit '' Set.range
          (fun u : (integralClosure ℤ_[p] L)ˣ => ((u : integralClosure ℤ_[p] L) : L)) ⊆
        {z : L | ‖z‖ ≤ (p : ℝ) ^ (Proposition1_2.b p (P.ramificationIdx ℤ_[p]))} := by
  let := spectralNorm.normedField ℚ_[p] L
  have := isDedekindDomain_ringOfIntegers_padic p L
  have := isTorsionFree_ringOfIntegers_padic p L
  have he : 1 ≤ P.ramificationIdx ℤ_[p] :=
    ramificationIdx_pos_of_liesOver (IsDiscreteValuationRing.not_a_field ℤ_[p]) P
  rw [padicBridge_range_units_eq_unitSphere]
  exact extLogUnit_image_bounds_spectralNorm p L he (padicBridge_hval p L P)

/-- **IUT IV Proposition 1.2 (i) with fractional ideals** (page 10): there are `y`, `z` in `L`
with `ord(y) = a` and `ord(z) = -b` (that is `‖y‖ = p ^ (-a)`, `‖z‖ = p ^ b`), and for any such
`y`, `z` the fractional ideals `p ^ a · R = y · R` and `p ^ (-b) · R = z · R` satisfy
`y · R ⊆ log (R^×) ⊆ z · R`, with `R = integralClosure ℤ_[p] L` and `e = P.ramificationIdx`. -/
theorem padicBridge_extLogUnit_image_fractionalIdeal (P : Ideal (integralClosure ℤ_[p] L))
    [P.IsPrime] [P.LiesOver (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal ℤ_[p])] :
    letI := spectralNorm.normedField ℚ_[p] L
    (∃ y : L, ‖y‖ = (p : ℝ) ^ (-Proposition1_2.a p (P.ramificationIdx ℤ_[p]))) ∧
      (∃ z : L, ‖z‖ = (p : ℝ) ^ (Proposition1_2.b p (P.ramificationIdx ℤ_[p]))) ∧
      ∀ y z : L, ‖y‖ = (p : ℝ) ^ (-Proposition1_2.a p (P.ramificationIdx ℤ_[p])) →
        ‖z‖ = (p : ℝ) ^ (Proposition1_2.b p (P.ramificationIdx ℤ_[p])) →
        Set.range (fun r : integralClosure ℤ_[p] L => y * (r : L)) ⊆
            extLogUnit '' Set.range
              (fun u : (integralClosure ℤ_[p] L)ˣ => ((u : integralClosure ℤ_[p] L) : L)) ∧
          extLogUnit '' Set.range
              (fun u : (integralClosure ℤ_[p] L)ˣ => ((u : integralClosure ℤ_[p] L) : L)) ⊆
            Set.range (fun r : integralClosure ℤ_[p] L => z * (r : L)) := by
  let := spectralNorm.normedField ℚ_[p] L
  have := isDedekindDomain_ringOfIntegers_padic p L
  have := isTorsionFree_ringOfIntegers_padic p L
  have he : 0 < P.ramificationIdx ℤ_[p] :=
    ramificationIdx_pos_of_liesOver (IsDiscreteValuationRing.not_a_field ℤ_[p]) P
  have hp0 : (0 : ℝ) < p := by exact_mod_cast (Fact.out : p.Prime).pos
  obtain ⟨ka, hka⟩ := padicBridge_a_eq_int_div p he.ne'
  obtain ⟨kb, hkb⟩ := padicBridge_b_eq_int_div p he.ne'
  obtain ⟨h1, h2⟩ := padicBridge_extLogUnit_image_bounds p L P
  refine ⟨?_, ?_, fun y z hy hz => ⟨?_, ?_⟩⟩
  · obtain ⟨y, -, hy⟩ := padicBridge_exists_norm_eq_rpow p L P (-ka)
    refine ⟨y, ?_⟩
    rw [hy, hka]
    push_cast
    ring_nf
  · obtain ⟨z, -, hz⟩ := padicBridge_exists_norm_eq_rpow p L P kb
    exact ⟨z, by rw [hz, hkb]⟩
  · have hy0 : y ≠ 0 := by
      intro h0
      rw [h0, norm_zero] at hy
      exact (Real.rpow_pos_of_pos hp0 _).ne' hy.symm
    rw [← padicBridge_closedBall_eq_range_mul p L hy0, hy]
    exact h1
  · have hz0 : z ≠ 0 := by
      intro h0
      rw [h0, norm_zero] at hz
      exact (Real.rpow_pos_of_pos hp0 _).ne' hz.symm
    rw [← padicBridge_closedBall_eq_range_mul p L hz0, hz]
    exact h2

/-- **IUT IV Proposition 1.2 (i), the equality case** (page 10): for `p > 2` and
`e ≤ p - 2`, `e = P.ramificationIdx ℤ_[p]`, `log (R^×) = p ^ (1 / e) · R`, written as the closed
ball `{‖z‖ ≤ p ^ (-1 / e)}`, with `R^×` the unit group of `integralClosure ℤ_[p] L`. -/
theorem padicBridge_extLogUnit_image_eq_of_le (P : Ideal (integralClosure ℤ_[p] L)) [P.IsPrime]
    [P.LiesOver (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal ℤ_[p])] (hp2 : 2 < p) (hep : P.ramificationIdx ℤ_[p] ≤ p - 2) :
    letI := spectralNorm.normedField ℚ_[p] L
    extLogUnit '' Set.range
        (fun u : (integralClosure ℤ_[p] L)ˣ => ((u : integralClosure ℤ_[p] L) : L)) =
      {z : L | ‖z‖ ≤ (p : ℝ) ^ (-(1 / (P.ramificationIdx ℤ_[p] : ℝ)))} := by
  let := spectralNorm.normedField ℚ_[p] L
  have := isDedekindDomain_ringOfIntegers_padic p L
  have := isTorsionFree_ringOfIntegers_padic p L
  have he : 1 ≤ P.ramificationIdx ℤ_[p] :=
    ramificationIdx_pos_of_liesOver (IsDiscreteValuationRing.not_a_field ℤ_[p]) P
  obtain ⟨ha, hb⟩ := Proposition1_2.a_b_of_le hp2 he hep
  have h := padicBridge_extLogUnit_image_bounds p L P
  rw [ha, hb] at h
  exact Set.Subset.antisymm h.2 h.1

/-- **The log-shell bounds** given by IUT IV Proposition 1.2 (i), for a finite extension `L` of
`ℚ_[p]`: `p* p ^ a · R ⊆ I ⊆ p* p ^ (-b) · R` (closed balls of radii `p* p ^ (-a)` and
`p* p ^ b`), with `I = extLogShell p L` the log-shell of IUT III Definition 1.1, whose units are
the unit group of `integralClosure ℤ_[p] L` (`padicBridge_range_units_eq_unitSphere`), and
`e = P.ramificationIdx ℤ_[p]`. -/
theorem padicBridge_extLogShell_bounds (P : Ideal (integralClosure ℤ_[p] L)) [P.IsPrime]
    [P.LiesOver (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal ℤ_[p])] :
    letI := spectralNorm.normedField ℚ_[p] L
    {y : L | ‖y‖ ≤ ((IUT.Prerequisites.PadicLog.padicLogPStar p : ℕ) : ℝ) *
        (p : ℝ) ^ (-Proposition1_2.a p (P.ramificationIdx ℤ_[p]))} ⊆ extLogShell p L ∧
      extLogShell p L ⊆ {y : L | ‖y‖ ≤ ((IUT.Prerequisites.PadicLog.padicLogPStar p : ℕ) : ℝ) *
        (p : ℝ) ^ (Proposition1_2.b p (P.ramificationIdx ℤ_[p]))} := by
  let := spectralNorm.normedField ℚ_[p] L
  let := spectralNorm.normedAlgebra ℚ_[p] L
  have := isDedekindDomain_ringOfIntegers_padic p L
  have := isTorsionFree_ringOfIntegers_padic p L
  have : CompleteSpace L := FiniteDimensional.completeSpace ℚ_[p] L
  have : ProperSpace L := FiniteDimensional.proper ℚ_[p] L
  have he : 1 ≤ P.ramificationIdx ℤ_[p] :=
    ramificationIdx_pos_of_liesOver (IsDiscreteValuationRing.not_a_field ℤ_[p]) P
  exact extLogShell_bounds p he (padicBridge_hval p L P)

/-- **Proposition 1.2 (i) together with the different** (pages 10 to 12): for the prime `P` over
`p` of `R = integralClosure ℤ_[p] L` (the only one, `padicBridge_prime_eq_maximalIdeal`), with
`e = P.ramificationIdx ℤ_[p]` and `𝔡 = differentOrder ℤ_[p] R P`: the inclusions
`p ^ a · R ⊆ log (R^×) ⊆ p ^ (-b) · R` (closed-ball form), `𝔡 ≥ (e - 1) / e`
(Proposition 1.3 (i) for `k_0 = ℚ_p`), and `𝔡 + a ≥ 1` if `p > 2`, `𝔡 + a ≥ 2` if `p = 2`
(used on page 14 in the proof of Proposition 1.4 (iii)), all with the same `e`. -/
theorem padicBridge_log_bounds_and_differentOrder (P : Ideal (integralClosure ℤ_[p] L))
    [P.IsPrime] [P.LiesOver (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal ℤ_[p])] :
    letI := spectralNorm.normedField ℚ_[p] L
    letI := isDedekindDomain_ringOfIntegers_padic p L
    letI := isTorsionFree_ringOfIntegers_padic p L
    ({z : L | ‖z‖ ≤ (p : ℝ) ^ (-Proposition1_2.a p (P.ramificationIdx ℤ_[p]))} ⊆
        extLogUnit '' Set.range
          (fun u : (integralClosure ℤ_[p] L)ˣ => ((u : integralClosure ℤ_[p] L) : L)) ∧
      extLogUnit '' Set.range
          (fun u : (integralClosure ℤ_[p] L)ˣ => ((u : integralClosure ℤ_[p] L) : L)) ⊆
        {z : L | ‖z‖ ≤ (p : ℝ) ^ (Proposition1_2.b p (P.ramificationIdx ℤ_[p]))}) ∧
      ((P.ramificationIdx ℤ_[p] : ℝ) - 1) / P.ramificationIdx ℤ_[p] ≤
        differentOrder ℤ_[p] (integralClosure ℤ_[p] L) P ∧
      (2 < p → 1 ≤ differentOrder ℤ_[p] (integralClosure ℤ_[p] L) P +
        Proposition1_2.a p (P.ramificationIdx ℤ_[p])) ∧
      (p = 2 → 2 ≤ differentOrder ℤ_[p] (integralClosure ℤ_[p] L) P +
        Proposition1_2.a p (P.ramificationIdx ℤ_[p])) :=
  ⟨padicBridge_extLogUnit_image_bounds p L P, padic_differentOrder_ge p L P,
    (padic_differentOrder_add_a_ge p L P).1, (padic_differentOrder_add_a_ge p L P).2⟩

end Bridge

end IUT.PaperIV.LocalFields
